      "text": "To evaluate \\(\\left\\lfloor -\\frac{5}{3} \\right\\rfloor\\), we first need to find the value of \\(-\\frac{5}{3}\\).\n\n\\[\n-\\frac{5}{3} \\approx -1.6667\n\\]\n\nThe floor function \\(\\left\\lfloor x \\right\\rfloor\\) returns the greatest integer less than or equal to \\(x\\). For \\(x = -1.6667\\), the greatest integer less than or equal to \\(-1.6667\\) is \\(-2\\).\n\nTherefore, \\(\\left\\lfloor -\\frac{5}{3} \\right\\rfloor = -2\\).\n\nLet's confirm this using Python code.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Calculate the floor of -5/3\nvalue = -5 / 3\nfloor_value = math.floor(value)\nprint(floor_value)\n```\n```output\n-2\n```\nThe final answer is \\(\\boxed{-2}\\).",
